<title>POLAND: FRANCE TO HELP POLAND UNDERSTAND EU LAWS.</title>
<headline>FRANCE TO HELP POLAND UNDERSTAND EU LAWS.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-02-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Polish and French justice ministers on Friday signed a cooperation agreement, which provides for training Polish judges in the European Union law, PAP news agency reported.</p>
<p>PAP said the accord, signed by France's Jacques Toubon and his Polish counterpart Leszek Kubicki, also envisaged French help in introducing computer techonology to Polish courts.</p>
<p>Kubicki was quoted as saying that French experts will offer the Euroepan law courses to about 3,500 Polish judges over the next two years.</p>
</text>
